      "error": null,
      "answer": {
        "answer": "RuptureOps cannot currently be released publicly as the existing repository or benchmark fixture. A public build should be a clean artifact containing independently authored implementation only, with no SRDB-derived corpus/assets or personalized material. Generated icon and audio files need provenance and license review before inclusion. Broader distribution requires written source-owner permission or replacement with separately licensed data.",
        "claims": [
          {
            "id": "c1",
            "value": "SRDB permits crawling, but its footer asserts copyright and it publishes no explicit content/data reuse license. Therefore the mirrored raw archive, normalized corpus, derived SQLite database, images, icons, and other mirrored source assets remain private research material and are not cleared for republication.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/docs/data-corpus.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c2",
            "value": "Private personalized material includes the imported package and duplicate third-party corpus, exact player prompt histories, personalized save state and models, screenshots and site images, player planning notes, conversation-derived decisions, maps/site context, vault knowledge, saved scenarios, and generated player-specific outputs. The benchmark fixture combines this personal play state with third-party-derived material and must not be published.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/docs/data-corpus.md",
              "Topics/StarRupture/Knowledge base and modeling.md",
              "CORPUS.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c3",
            "value": "The current corpus-bearing repository is not itself public-release-safe. A public build can presently use only a separately packaged, independently authored implementation that excludes raw and normalized snapshots, SQLite, source-derived facts and text, mirrored site images/icons, imports, models, screenshots, and other player artifacts. The generated app icon and warning audio occur inside the explicitly private benchmark fixture; because the retrieved evidence contains no distribution license or provenance clearance for those binaries, treat them as private pending review rather than assuming they may ship.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/docs/data-corpus.md",
              "CORPUS.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          },
          {
            "id": "c4",
            "value": "Safe broader distribution requires either written reuse permission from the source owner covering the dataset, text, images/icons, mirrored assets, normalized and derived forms, and app distribution, or adoption of a different independently obtained and separately licensed data strategy. Before release, establish an explicit allowlist for independently authored code and cleared original assets, review every image/icon/audio file\u2019s provenance and license, and enforce exclusions for private corpus and player material.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/docs/data-corpus.md",
              "Topics/StarRupture/Knowledge base and modeling.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ],
        "checkpoint": {
          "objective": "Prepare an evidence-backed public-release data and asset boundary for RuptureOps.",
          "current_state": [
            "Verified against base corpus revision revision:019f567a47b573a0b04b16339849868d that SRDB has no explicit data/content reuse license and asserts copyright.",
            "Verified that raw captures, mirrored assets, normalized snapshots, SQLite, imported personalized material, and the benchmark fixture remain private.",
            "Verified that the existing repository co-locates implementation and private corpus material and is documented as private.",
            "Checkpoint persisted as checkpoint:019f567b-3fba-7773-a244-c8e0c9bd10f6."
          ],
          "decisions": [
            "Treat the existing repository and benchmark fixture as non-public.",
            "Treat a clean, independently authored implementation-only artifact as the current public-build path.",
            "Treat generated icon and warning audio as uncleared until provenance and distribution rights are verified.",
            "Do not infer that provenance labeling makes promoted source-derived facts redistributable."
          ],
          "open_questions": [
            "Whether written permission can be obtained from the SRDB owner and what uses it would cover.",
            "Whether generated app icon and warning audio have provenance and license records permitting public distribution.",
            "Which alternate licensed or first-party dataset could replace SRDB-derived content."
          ],
          "next_actions": [
            "Request written source-owner permission or select a separately licensed dataset.",
            "Create a public artifact allowlist and automated denylist checks for corpus, database, imports, models, screenshots, prompt history, vault material, and generated player outputs.",
            "Perform asset-by-asset provenance and license review for every image, icon, and audio file.",
            "Package independently authored implementation separately from the private research repository."
          ],
